From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Fri, 12 Jun 2026 19:34:46 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] patch 0219 -- T48 iter-8: WB GS-reset synth (opt-in) +
 DRR-cap witness + teardown banner fix

iter-7 proved the cold-init reorder kills the WaveBlaster freeze on the
g2k DX2-66 (159 s no-wedge). iter-8 is the audio-COHERENCE layer. This is
the engine half (Lever B + the shared witnesses); sdl-engine's SDL/0097
is Lever A (per-byte bit-6 DRR poll restore + the drr_cap counters).

LEVER B -- GS-reset synth (opt-in, default OFF): the Dream SAM2695's
power-up voice map is not GM-grand-piano ("cowbell/wrong voice", the H11
boot map). A GM/GS/XG reset SysEx switches it, but MidiScheduler discards
stream SysEx (MidiScheduler.cpp:976-991) so none from the .mid ever
reaches the daughterboard. New hint SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_AUDIO_WB_VOICE_RESET
= gs|xg|gm|none (default none): at on_song_start the WB backend
synthesizes the chosen reset SysEx (GS lead = F0 41 10 42 12 40 00 7F 00
41 F7) FIRST, before the all-notes-off and the song's program-changes, so
the chip is on the requested map when those program-changes land. The
emit is pacing-agnostic -- it writes via SDL_DOSMpu401WriteByte, so it
composes with whichever SDL pacing (DRR poll OR timed-delay) is active.
Resets were "ignored" in WBTEST-003 only under the no-poll OVERRUN regime;
SDL/0097's pacing removes the overrun, so they may now land.

WITNESSES (flush-instr iter-8 CONTRACT):
- 2.2 GS-reset landed-witness: "WB GS-reset: K bytes SysEx + P
  program-changes sent to 0x330, drr_cap_hits_during_reset=R" once at
  song-start. K = sysex length (GS=11). P=0 (the lever sends only the
  reset; the .mid's own program-changes select voices). R = drr_cap_hits
  delta across the reset -- R~0 = landed cleanly (Lever B creditable),
  R high = the reset overran (INVALID-for-B). (Under timed-delay pacing
  drr_cap_hits stays 0, so R=0 is trivial there -- the dispatch climb +
  ear are the landed-proof on that path.)
- 2.1 drr_cap_hits dispatch tail: appended to the existing N=8 main-line
  dispatch line -- "...; drr_cap_hits=C (pct% of bytes capped, cap=B)".
  ~0% = the restored poll paces cleanly; ~100% = chip persistently busy =
  latency-drag (looks like a hang without being a true wedge). Reads
  sdl-engine SDL/0097's doskutsu_mpu_drr_cap_hits + doskutsu_mpu_drr_cap.

LEVER C cosmetic (sdl-engine's diagnosis): silence_for_shutdown's
"via DSP cmd 0x38" banner was a stale patch-0136 hardcoded string -- the
CC123 actually routes via the direct-port transport (s_mpu401_use_dsp is
false through teardown), the SAME as play. The wave-41 hanging note was
the H20 blind-write overrun, fixed for free by the poll, NOT a transport
mismatch. Corrected the banner text; no behavior change.

Combined-build symbols: doskutsu_mpu_drr_cap_hits + doskutsu_mpu_drr_cap
from SDL/0097 (links clean against the rebuilt sysroot).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>
